// Windows-only native FFI smoke: per-symbol DLL via `@ffi.link("...")` (portable form).
//
// This verifies that:
// - `@ffi.link("...")` is treated as if the user passed `--link ...`,
// - Windows x64 FFI resolver searches those DLLs without requiring explicit `--link`,
// - a program can call a symbol from a non-kernel32 DLL via this portable attribute.
//
// It is compiled+run only for x64-windows via `scripts/verify_native_matrix.sh`.

@ffi.link("msvcrt.dll")
ffi puts

var rc = puts("hello from msvcrt (via ffi.link)")
if rc < 0 { exit(1) }
exit(0)

